# Aether Vetted-Partner Source-Available License v1.0
## (Aether-VPSL-1.0)

Copyright © 2026 The Aether Consortium (the "Licensor").
All rights reserved.

This software, including its source code, object code,
schemas, reference plugins, contract packages, fitness
checks, documentation, and any accompanying materials
(collectively, the "Software"), is the work of the
Licensor and is made available under this License.

This Software is a dual-use engineering platform developed
under the European Innovation Council (EIC) Pathfinder
programme within Horizon Europe, Grant Agreement reference
as recorded in the accompanying grant documentation. The
Licensor has elected to release the source code for the
purposes of collaborative development, conformance testing,
and security review by named partners only.

---

## 1. Definitions

1.1. "Vetted Partner" means a natural person, legal
entity, or organisational unit that has been (a) admitted
to the Aether Consortium under the EIC Pathfinder Grant
Agreement, (b) named in the Vetted Partner Register
maintained by the Licensor at the canonical project
repository (the "Register", published in the file
`PARTNERS.md` at the root of the canonical project
repository), and (c) bound by a written
vetted-partner agreement with the Licensor that includes
confidentiality, use-restriction, and export-control
obligations at least as protective as this License.

1.2. "Permitted Use" means any use of the Software that
is (a) made by a Vetted Partner, (b) made in the course
of the Aether Consortium's work under the EIC Pathfinder
Grant Agreement, and (c) not prohibited by Section 3.

1.3. "Affiliates" of a Vetted Partner means entities
controlling, controlled by, or under common control with
that Vetted Partner, where "control" means ownership of
more than fifty percent (50%) of the voting equity.

1.4. **Initial Vetted Partners.** The following EU
partners of the Aether Consortium are named in the
Register as Vetted Partners as of the date of this
License:

- **Addcomposites Oy** (Finland);
- **Institut national polytechnique de Toulouse**
  (National Polytechnic Institute of Toulouse) (France).

Admission, cessation, and register administration follow
Sections 1.1 and 8.3.

